## actions.json Structure

Each action has: display_name, description, parameters (JSON Schema), response (JSON Schema).

### Parameters Schema
- ✅ Flat preferred: string, number, integer, boolean
- ✅ Arrays of primitives allowed: `"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}`
- ✅ Use `$schema`: "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
- ✅ All properties need `description`
- ❌ Avoid nested objects in parameters - flatten or construct in server.js

### Response Schema
- ✅ Nested objects allowed
- ✅ Arrays allowed
- ✅ Use `additionalProperties: true` for flexible API responses
- ✅ Include essential fields only

### Example
```json
{
  "getResource": {
    "display_name": "Get Resource",
    "description": "Retrieve a resource by ID",
    "parameters": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "resource_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Resource ID" }
      },
      "required": ["resource_id"]
    },
    "response": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "properties": {
        "id": { "type": "string" },
        "status": { "type": "string" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

